# AI Reviewer Subsystem

Automated QA scoring of submissions via LLMs, with calibration, golden sets,
rule packs, and cost/budget guards.

## Backend map (`backend/src/services/`)

- `AIReviewerService.ts` — the orchestrator. By far the largest service in the
  tree and a known refactor target: when you touch it, extract cohesive units (prompt assembly,
  reconciliation, self-consistency/voting, cost gating) into siblings rather
  than growing it. Do not add large new blocks inline.
- `aiReviewerPrompt.ts`, `aiReviewerTwoPassPrompts.ts`, `aiReviewerPromptAddenda.ts`
  — prompt construction.
- `aiReviewerTraceVoting.ts`, `aiReviewerPivotDetector.ts` — self-consistency / trace logic.
- `AIReviewerCostGuard.ts` — token/cost budget enforcement.
- `ai/` — model clients (`OpenAIClient.ts`, `AnthropicClient.ts`, `ChatModelClient.ts`, `AnswersToolSchema.ts`).
- Extensive `services/__tests__/aiReviewer*` and `AIReviewerService.*` Vitest suites — keep them green; add tests when you split the orchestrator.

Routes live in `backend/src/routes/ai-reviewer.routes.ts` (also oversized —
handlers should move into controllers/services, not stay inline in the route file).

## Frontend map (`frontend/src/pages/quality/ai-reviewer/`)

Settings/detail is composed of small cards (`SamplingCard`, `BudgetCard`,
`ModelProviderCard`, `GuidanceRulesCard`, `QuestionRubricsCard`, `GoldenSetCard`,
`CalibrationMetricsPanel`, etc.). Follow this card pattern; mirror an existing
card and obey the UI rules in [.cursor/rules/ui-design.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/ui-design.mdc).

